Native messaging starts Apple Passwords' helper (com.apple.passwordmanager) only from Ardia's own host directory. The
helper's launch constraint kills it at exec (SIGKILL, Code Signature Invalid) unless its parent is a browser Apple lists
or one signed with com.apple.developer.web-browser.public-key-credential, so every connectNative from the iCloud
Passwords extension left a PasswordManagerBrowserExtensionHelper crash report, every few minutes, once Helium's
scan-chrome-native-messaging-hosts found Apple's manifest in /Library/Google/Chrome/NativeMessagingHosts. ArdiaCore
(ACNativeMessaging.mm) writes the manifest into <user data dir>/NativeMessagingHosts only when the app holds that
entitlement, so FindManifest looks for this host there and nowhere else, and answers "Can't find native messaging host"
otherwise.

